var ANS={"Nov25 Q1": "<p><b>&lt;img&gt;<\/b>. It is an empty tag: <code>&lt;img src=\"logo.png\" alt=\"College logo\"&gt;<\/code>. <code>src<\/code> gives the file, <code>alt<\/code> the text shown if the image cannot load.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q2": "<p>A <b>block<\/b> element starts on a new line and takes the full width (<code>&lt;div&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;p&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;h1&gt;<\/code>). An <b>inline<\/b> element stays in the line and takes only the width of its content (<code>&lt;span&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;a&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;b&gt;<\/code>).<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;p&gt;This is a block. &lt;span&gt;This span stays inline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<\/pre>", "Nov25 Q3": "<p><b>padding<\/b>, e.g. <code>padding: 10px;<\/code>. (margin is the space <i>outside<\/i> the border.)<\/p>", "Nov25 Q4": "<p><b>opacity<\/b> sets how transparent an element is, from 0 (fully transparent) to 1 (fully opaque). <code>img { opacity: 0.5; }<\/code> makes the image half see-through.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q5": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const pi = 3.14;<\/pre>", "Nov25 Q6": "<p><b>val()<\/b> gets or sets the value of a form field. <code>$(\"#name\").val()<\/code> reads what the user typed; <code>$(\"#name\").val(\"Ravi\")<\/code> sets it.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q7": "<p><b>btn btn-primary<\/b>: <code>&lt;button class=\"btn btn-primary\"&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;<\/code><\/p>", "Nov25 Q8": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"jsx\">function Greet() {\n  return &lt;p&gt;Hi there!&lt;/p&gt;;\n}<\/pre>", "Nov25 Q9": "<p>It deletes the <b>first<\/b> document in the <code>products<\/code> collection whose <code>productID<\/code> is <code>\"P101\"<\/code>. Only one document is removed even if several match; it returns <code>{ acknowledged: true, deletedCount: 1 }<\/code> (0 if none matched).<\/p>", "Nov25 Q10": "<p><b>listen()<\/b>: <code>app.listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(\"Server running on port 3000\"));<\/code> starts the Express server on port 3000.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q11": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Home&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h1&gt;Hello World!&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Learning HTML is fun!&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;img src=&quot;banner.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Homepage Banner&quot;&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>&lt;h1&gt;<\/code> gives the heading, <code>&lt;p&gt;<\/code> the paragraph and <code>&lt;img&gt;<\/code> the image, with <code>alt<\/code> shown when banner.jpg is missing (as in the preview).<\/p>", "Nov25 Q12": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  h1 {\n    color: maroon;\n    font-size: 24px;\n    background-color: beige;\n  }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;h1&gt;Styled Heading&lt;/h1&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The selector <code>h1<\/code> picks every heading; each property is written <code>property: value;<\/code> inside the braces.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q13": "<p>All three use the anchor tag <code>&lt;a&gt;<\/code>; only the <code>href<\/code> changes.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>External website<\/b>: <code>href<\/code> is a full URL. <code>target=\"_blank\"<\/code> opens it in a new tab.<\/li>\n<li><b>Email link<\/b>: <code>href=\"mailto:…\"<\/code> opens the user's mail app with the address filled in.<\/li>\n<li><b>Phone link<\/b>: <code>href=\"tel:…\"<\/code> starts a call on a phone.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.karunya.edu&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Visit Karunya&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:admin@karunya.edu&quot;&gt;Email the admin&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;tel:+919876543210&quot;&gt;Call us&lt;/a&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "Nov25 Q14": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script&gt;\n  function showMessage() {\n    alert(&quot;Submission Successful!&quot;);\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;button onclick=&quot;showMessage()&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>The function is declared with <code>function<\/code>, and <code>alert()<\/code> shows the message box. Here it is called when the button is clicked.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q15": "<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>find()<\/th><th>findOne()<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Returns <b>all<\/b> documents that match the filter<\/td><td>Returns only the <b>first<\/b> matching document<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Returns a <b>cursor<\/b> (shown as an array of documents)<\/td><td>Returns a single <b>document<\/b>, or <code>null<\/code> if none match<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Used to list records<\/td><td>Used to fetch one record, e.g. by id<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">db.students.find({ dept: &quot;CSE&quot; })        // every CSE student\ndb.students.findOne({ dept: &quot;CSE&quot; })     // only the first CSE student\ndb.students.findOne({ regno: &quot;URK24CS1021&quot; })   // one student by id<\/pre>", "Nov25 Q16": "<p>Load the built-in <b>fs<\/b> (file system) module with <code>require<\/code>, then call <code>writeFile<\/code>. It creates output.txt (or overwrites it) and calls the callback when done.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const fs = require(&quot;fs&quot;);\n\nfs.writeFile(&quot;output.txt&quot;, &quot;Hello World&quot;, (err) =&gt; {\n  if (err) throw err;\n  console.log(&quot;File written successfully&quot;);\n});<\/pre>\n<p>Run it with <code>node write.js<\/code>. <code>fs.writeFileSync(\"output.txt\", \"Hello World\")<\/code> does the same job synchronously.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q17": "<p>The form groups related inputs in <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;<\/code>, ties every input to a <code>&lt;label&gt;<\/code> (accessibility), and uses HTML5 validation (<code>required<\/code>, <code>type=\"email\"<\/code>, <code>pattern<\/code>, <code>minlength<\/code>).<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Course Registration Portal&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #f2f4f8; }\n    form { width: 460px; margin: 20px auto; background: white; padding: 20px;\n           border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 8px; }\n    h2 { text-align: center; color: #1a3d7c; }\n    fieldset { border: 1px solid #ddd; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n    label { display: block; margin-top: 8px; font-weight: bold; }\n    input[type=text], input[type=email], input[type=password],\n    input[type=date], select, textarea { width: 100%; padding: 6px; box-sizing: border-box; }\n    .inline label { display: inline; font-weight: normal; margin-right: 10px; }\n    button { padding: 8px 18px; margin-top: 12px; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;form action=&quot;/register&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Course Registration Portal&lt;/h2&gt;\n\n    &lt;fieldset&gt;\n      &lt;legend&gt;Student Details&lt;/legend&gt;\n      &lt;label for=&quot;sname&quot;&gt;Student Name&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;sname&quot; name=&quot;sname&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter your full name&quot; required&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;email&quot;&gt;Email Address&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;email&quot; id=&quot;email&quot; name=&quot;email&quot; placeholder=&quot;name@example.com&quot; required&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;regno&quot;&gt;Registration Number&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;regno&quot; name=&quot;regno&quot; placeholder=&quot;e.g. URK24CS1021&quot;\n             pattern=&quot;[A-Z]{3}[0-9]{2}[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{4}&quot; required&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;pwd&quot;&gt;Password&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;password&quot; id=&quot;pwd&quot; name=&quot;pwd&quot; minlength=&quot;8&quot;\n             placeholder=&quot;At least 8 characters, with a number&quot; required&gt;\n    &lt;/fieldset&gt;\n\n    &lt;fieldset&gt;\n      &lt;legend&gt;Course Details&lt;/legend&gt;\n      &lt;label for=&quot;course&quot;&gt;Course&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;select id=&quot;course&quot; name=&quot;course&quot; required&gt;\n        &lt;option value=&quot;&quot;&gt;-- Select a course --&lt;/option&gt;\n        &lt;option&gt;Web Development&lt;/option&gt;\n        &lt;option&gt;Data Science&lt;/option&gt;\n        &lt;option&gt;Cybersecurity&lt;/option&gt;\n        &lt;option&gt;AI &amp;amp; ML&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;/select&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;start&quot;&gt;Course Start Date&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;date&quot; id=&quot;start&quot; name=&quot;start&quot; required&gt;\n\n      &lt;label&gt;Mode of Learning&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;inline&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;online&quot; name=&quot;mode&quot; value=&quot;Online&quot; required&gt;&lt;label for=&quot;online&quot;&gt;Online&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;offline&quot; name=&quot;mode&quot; value=&quot;Offline&quot;&gt;&lt;label for=&quot;offline&quot;&gt;Offline&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; id=&quot;hybrid&quot; name=&quot;mode&quot; value=&quot;Hybrid&quot;&gt;&lt;label for=&quot;hybrid&quot;&gt;Hybrid&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n\n      &lt;label for=&quot;goals&quot;&gt;Remarks / Learning Goals&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;textarea id=&quot;goals&quot; name=&quot;goals&quot; rows=&quot;3&quot; placeholder=&quot;What do you want to learn?&quot;&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;\n\n      &lt;div class=&quot;inline&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;sub&quot; name=&quot;subscribe&quot; checked&gt;\n        &lt;label for=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;Subscribe to course updates and notifications&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/fieldset&gt;\n\n    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button type=&quot;reset&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><b>How each element is used:<\/b><\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Element<\/th><th>Tag and attributes<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Text boxes<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"text\"&gt;<\/code> and <code>type=\"email\"<\/code> (the browser checks the @ format); <code>pattern<\/code> checks the register number format<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Password<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"password\" minlength=\"8\"&gt;<\/code>, characters are hidden<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Date selector<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"date\"&gt;<\/code> shows a calendar picker<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Text area<\/td><td><code>&lt;textarea rows=\"3\"&gt;<\/code> for multi-line remarks<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Check box<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"checkbox\"&gt;<\/code>, can be ticked on or off<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Radio buttons<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"radio\"&gt;<\/code> with the <b>same name<\/b>, so only one can be chosen<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Dropdown<\/td><td><code>&lt;select&gt;<\/code> with <code>&lt;option&gt;<\/code>s; the empty first option plus <code>required<\/code> forces a choice<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Buttons<\/td><td><code>type=\"submit\"<\/code> sends the form to <code>action<\/code> by <code>method<\/code>; <code>type=\"reset\"<\/code> clears it<\/td><\/tr>\n<\/table>\n<p><code>required<\/code> stops submission while a field is empty; <code>&lt;label for&gt;<\/code> lets a screen reader (and a click) find each field; <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;<\/code> and <code>&lt;legend&gt;<\/code> give the semantic grouping.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q18a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Seminar Timetable&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; }\n    th, td { padding: 8px 14px; text-align: center; }\n    th { background-color: #d9e2f3; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;table&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;th colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Seminar Timetable&lt;/th&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Day 1&lt;/th&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Day 2&lt;/th&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Welcome Address (9:00 - 9:30 AM)&lt;/td&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Web Technologies&lt;br&gt;9:30 - 11:00 AM&lt;br&gt;Dr. Ravi Kumar&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Cloud Computing&lt;br&gt;9:30 - 11:00 AM&lt;br&gt;Dr. Anitha S&lt;/td&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Artificial Intelligence&lt;br&gt;11:30 AM - 1:00 PM&lt;br&gt;Prof. John Paul&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Cyber Security&lt;br&gt;11:30 AM - 1:00 PM&lt;br&gt;Prof. Meena R&lt;/td&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Borders<\/b>: <code>border<\/code> on table, th and td; <code>border-collapse: collapse<\/code> merges double lines into one.<\/li>\n<li><b>Header row<\/b>: <code>&lt;th colspan=\"2\"&gt;<\/code> makes \"Seminar Timetable\" span both columns.<\/li>\n<li><b>Day labels<\/b>: second row of <code>&lt;th&gt;<\/code> cells.<\/li>\n<li><b>Merged session<\/b>: <code>&lt;td colspan=\"2\"&gt;<\/code> for \"Welcome Address\".<\/li>\n<li><b>Rows 4 and 5<\/b>: one session per day, each cell giving the session name, time and speaker.<\/li>\n<li><code>rowspan<\/code> merges cells vertically, e.g. <code>&lt;td rowspan=\"2\"&gt;Lunch&lt;/td&gt;<\/code> would cover two rows of one column. This layout only needs colspan.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Nov25 Q18b": "<p>The <code>position<\/code> property decides how an element is placed. The default is <code>static<\/code> (normal flow).<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Relative<\/b>: the element stays in the normal flow (its space is kept), but is shifted from <b>where it would normally be<\/b> by top/left/right/bottom.<\/li>\n<li><b>Absolute<\/b>: the element is taken <b>out<\/b> of the normal flow (other elements close the gap) and placed relative to its <b>nearest positioned ancestor<\/b> (one with position other than static), or the page if there is none.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Applied to the timetable: the table is made <code>relative<\/code> and moved 20px right and 10px down; a \"NEW\" badge is placed with <code>absolute<\/code> at the table's top-right corner. Because the table is positioned, the badge is measured from the table, not from the page.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    table, th, td { border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; }\n    th, td { padding: 8px 14px; text-align: center; }\n\n    /* (i) relative: moved from its normal place, space still reserved */\n    .timetable {\n      position: relative;\n      top: 10px;\n      left: 20px;\n    }\n\n    /* (ii) absolute: placed inside the nearest positioned ancestor (the table) */\n    .badge {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: -12px;\n      right: -12px;\n      background: red;\n      color: white;\n      padding: 3px 8px;\n      border-radius: 10px;\n      font-size: 12px;\n    }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;table class=&quot;timetable&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Seminar Timetable &lt;span class=&quot;badge&quot;&gt;NEW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Day 1&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Day 2&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Welcome Address&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Web Technologies&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Cloud Computing&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Artificial Intelligence&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Cyber Security&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/table&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th><\/th><th>Relative<\/th><th>Absolute<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>In normal flow?<\/td><td>Yes, its space is kept<\/td><td>No, removed from flow<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Offsets measured from<\/td><td>its own normal position<\/td><td>nearest positioned ancestor<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Typical use<\/td><td>small nudges; acting as the container for absolute children<\/td><td>badges, tooltips, overlays<\/td><\/tr><\/table>", "Nov25 Q19a": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    .card {\n      width: 300px;\n      padding: 15px;\n      margin: 20px;\n      border: 2px solid #1a3d7c;\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      background-color: #ffffff;\n      transition: background-color 0.5s ease;\n    }\n    .card:hover {\n      background-color: #dbe9ff;\n    }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;card&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Student Information&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Name:&lt;/b&gt; Ananya R&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reg No:&lt;/b&gt; URK24CS1021&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Department:&lt;/b&gt; CSE&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>width: 300px<\/code>, <code>padding: 15px<\/code> (inside the border), <code>margin: 20px<\/code> (outside the border) and <code>border: 2px solid<\/code> follow the box model: content → padding → border → margin.<\/li>\n<li><code>:hover<\/code> applies the new background when the mouse is over the card.<\/li>\n<li><code>transition: background-color 0.5s ease<\/code> makes the colour change smoothly over half a second instead of instantly. Hover over the preview to see it.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Nov25 Q19b": "<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Travel World&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Popular Travel Destinations&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Paris\n      &lt;ol&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Eiffel Tower&lt;/li&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Louvre Museum&lt;/li&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Notre-Dame&lt;/li&gt;\n      &lt;/ol&gt;\n    &lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Tokyo&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Dubai&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code> gives a bulleted (unordered) list, since the destinations have no order. The attractions are ranked, so they use <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code> (numbered). The nested <code>&lt;ol&gt;<\/code> must sit <b>inside<\/b> Paris's <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code>, before its closing tag, not directly inside the <code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q20": "<p>Kilogram = Grams / 1000.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Grams to Kilograms&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }\n    .box { width: 320px; margin: 20px auto; padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 8px; }\n    input { width: 100%; padding: 6px; box-sizing: border-box; }\n    button { margin-top: 10px; padding: 6px 14px; }\n    #result { margin-top: 12px; font-weight: bold; }\n    .error { color: red; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Weight Converter&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;form id=&quot;convForm&quot; onsubmit=&quot;return false;&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;label for=&quot;grams&quot;&gt;Weight in grams&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;grams&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter weight in grams&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; onclick=&quot;convert()&quot;&gt;Convert&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;reset&quot; onclick=&quot;clearResult()&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n    &lt;div id=&quot;result&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    function convert() {\n      var g = document.getElementById(&quot;grams&quot;).value.trim();\n      var out = document.getElementById(&quot;result&quot;);\n\n      if (g === &quot;&quot; || isNaN(g)) {\n        out.className = &quot;error&quot;;\n        out.innerHTML = &quot;Please enter a valid number.&quot;;\n        return;\n      }\n      if (Number(g) &lt; 0) {\n        out.className = &quot;error&quot;;\n        out.innerHTML = &quot;Weight cannot be negative.&quot;;\n        return;\n      }\n      var kg = Number(g) / 1000;\n      out.className = &quot;&quot;;\n      out.innerHTML = g + &quot; g = &quot; + kg + &quot; kg&quot;;\n    }\n\n    function clearResult() {\n      document.getElementById(&quot;result&quot;).innerHTML = &quot;&quot;;\n    }\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Text box<\/b> with the required placeholder; <b>Convert<\/b> calls <code>convert()<\/code>; <b>Reset<\/b> (<code>type=\"reset\"<\/code>) clears the box, and <code>clearResult()<\/code> clears the output.<\/li>\n<li><b>Validation<\/b>: empty input, non-numbers (<code>isNaN<\/code>) and negative values show a red error instead of a result.<\/li>\n<li><b>Dynamic output<\/b>: <code>innerHTML<\/code> of the result div is updated without reloading the page. Try 2500 in the preview, which gives 2.5 kg.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Nov25 Q21": "<p>The images start hidden with <code>display:none<\/code>, and each button calls one jQuery effect.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Product Showcase&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    .product { display: inline-block; width: 150px; margin: 10px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top; }\n    .product img { width: 140px; height: 100px; display: none; }\n    .desc { display: none; font-size: 13px; background: #eef; padding: 5px; }\n    button { margin: 3px; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Product Showcase&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;show&quot;&gt;Show&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;hide&quot;&gt;Hide&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;fadein&quot;&gt;Fade In&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;fadeout&quot;&gt;Fade Out&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;slidedown&quot;&gt;Slide Down&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=&quot;slideup&quot;&gt;Slide Up&lt;/button&gt;\n\n  &lt;div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;product&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;img src=&quot;https://picsum.photos/id/0/140/100&quot; alt=&quot;Laptop&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;desc&quot;&gt;Laptop - 16 GB RAM, 512 GB SSD&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;product&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;img src=&quot;https://picsum.photos/id/250/140/100&quot; alt=&quot;Camera&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;desc&quot;&gt;Camera - 24 MP, 4K video&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;product&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;img src=&quot;https://picsum.photos/id/96/140/100&quot; alt=&quot;Headphones&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;desc&quot;&gt;Headphones - wireless, noise cancelling&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    $(document).ready(function () {\n      $(&quot;#show&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.product img&quot;).show(); });\n      $(&quot;#hide&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.product img&quot;).hide(); });\n      $(&quot;#fadein&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.product img&quot;).fadeIn(1000); });\n      $(&quot;#fadeout&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.product img&quot;).fadeOut(1000); });\n      $(&quot;#slidedown&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.desc&quot;).slideDown(); });\n      $(&quot;#slideup&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;.desc&quot;).slideUp(); });\n    });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>What it does<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>show()<\/code> / <code>hide()<\/code><\/td><td>display or hide instantly (sets display)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>fadeIn(ms)<\/code> / <code>fadeOut(ms)<\/code><\/td><td>change opacity gradually over the given time, then show / hide<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>slideDown()<\/code> / <code>slideUp()<\/code><\/td><td>animate the height to reveal / hide, like a drawer<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><code>$(document).ready()<\/code> waits until the page has loaded before attaching the click handlers; <code>$(\".product img\")<\/code> selects all three images at once.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q22": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">// 1. object\nlet smartDevice = {\n  deviceName: &quot;Smartwatch X100&quot;,\n  deviceId: 102,\n  category: &quot;Wearables&quot;,\n  specs: [&quot;Heart Rate Monitor&quot;, &quot;GPS&quot;, &quot;Water Resistant&quot;],\n  available: false,\n  price: 14999.99\n};\n\n// 2. serialization: object -&gt; JSON string\nlet jsonStr = JSON.stringify(smartDevice);\nconsole.log(&quot;Serialized JSON:&quot;);\nconsole.log(jsonStr);\n\n// 3. deserialization: JSON string -&gt; object\nlet device = JSON.parse(jsonStr);\nconsole.log(&quot;Deserialized object:&quot;);\nconsole.log(device);\n\n// 4. read values from the object\nconsole.log(&quot;Device ID: &quot; + device.deviceId);\nconsole.log(&quot;Second spec: &quot; + device.specs[1]);\n\nif (device.price &gt; 10000) {\n  console.log(&quot;Over Priced&quot;);\n} else {\n  console.log(&quot;Normal Price&quot;);\n}<\/pre>\n<p><b>Output<\/b> (run with node):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">Serialized JSON:\n{&quot;deviceName&quot;:&quot;Smartwatch X100&quot;,&quot;deviceId&quot;:102,&quot;category&quot;:&quot;Wearables&quot;,&quot;specs&quot;:[&quot;Heart Rate Monitor&quot;,&quot;GPS&quot;,&quot;Water Resistant&quot;],&quot;available&quot;:false,&quot;price&quot;:14999.99}\nDeserialized object:\n{\n  deviceName: &#x27;Smartwatch X100&#x27;,\n  deviceId: 102,\n  category: &#x27;Wearables&#x27;,\n  specs: [ &#x27;Heart Rate Monitor&#x27;, &#x27;GPS&#x27;, &#x27;Water Resistant&#x27; ],\n  available: false,\n  price: 14999.99\n}\nDevice ID: 102\nSecond spec: GPS\nOver Priced<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Serialization<\/b>: <code>JSON.stringify()<\/code> turns the object into a string, so it can be stored or sent. Keys get double quotes.<\/li>\n<li><b>Deserialization<\/b>: <code>JSON.parse()<\/code> turns the string back into an object whose properties can be used.<\/li>\n<li>Arrays are zero-indexed, so the second spec is <code>specs[1]<\/code> = \"GPS\". 14999.99 &gt; 10000, so it prints \"Over Priced\".<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>To show it on the web page instead of the console, write each line with <code>document.getElementById(\"out\").innerHTML += …<\/code>.<\/p>", "Nov25 Q23": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">// i) create / switch to the database\nuse hospitalDB\n\n// ii) create the collection\ndb.createCollection(&quot;patients&quot;)\n\n// iii) insert 3 patients\ndb.patients.insertMany([\n  { patientID: &quot;P001&quot;, name: &quot;Arun Kumar&quot;, age: 45, department: &quot;Cardiology&quot;,\n    admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-11-02&quot;), dischargeDate: null, status: &quot;admitted&quot; },\n  { patientID: &quot;P002&quot;, name: &quot;Divya S&quot;, age: 32, department: &quot;Neurology&quot;,\n    admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-10-20&quot;), dischargeDate: new Date(&quot;2025-10-28&quot;), status: &quot;discharged&quot; },\n  { patientID: &quot;P003&quot;, name: &quot;Rahul M&quot;, age: 60, department: &quot;Orthopedics&quot;,\n    admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-11-05&quot;), dischargeDate: null, status: &quot;under observation&quot; }\n])\n\n// iv) one patient by patientID\ndb.patients.findOne({ patientID: &quot;P002&quot; })\n\n// v) delete a patient by patientID\ndb.patients.deleteOne({ patientID: &quot;P002&quot; })\n\n// vi) all Cardiology patients\ndb.patients.find({ department: &quot;Cardiology&quot; })\n\n// vii) add insuranceProvider to every patient\ndb.patients.updateMany({}, { $set: { insuranceProvider: &quot;Not Provided&quot; } })\n\n// viii) update a patient&#x27;s status\ndb.patients.updateOne({ patientID: &quot;P003&quot; }, { $set: { status: &quot;admitted&quot; } })\n\n// ix) name, department, status sorted by admissionDate (newest first)\ndb.patients.find({}, { name: 1, department: 1, status: 1, _id: 0 }).sort({ admissionDate: -1 })\n\n// x) count patients currently admitted\ndb.patients.countDocuments({ status: &quot;admitted&quot; })<\/pre>\n<p><b>Output<\/b> (run in mongosh):<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">test&gt; use hospitalDB\nswitched to db hospitalDB\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.createCollection(&quot;patients&quot;)\n{ ok: 1 }\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.insertMany([\n...   { patientID: &quot;P001&quot;, name: &quot;Arun Kumar&quot;, age: 45, department: &quot;Cardiology&quot;,\n...     admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-11-02&quot;), dischargeDate: null, status: &quot;admitted&quot; },\n...   { patientID: &quot;P002&quot;, name: &quot;Divya S&quot;, age: 32, department: &quot;Neurology&quot;,\n...     admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-10-20&quot;), dischargeDate: new Date(&quot;2025-10-28&quot;), status: &quot;discharged&quot; },\n...   { patientID: &quot;P003&quot;, name: &quot;Rahul M&quot;, age: 60, department: &quot;Orthopedics&quot;,\n...     admissionDate: new Date(&quot;2025-11-05&quot;), dischargeDate: null, status: &quot;under observation&quot; }\n... ])\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedIds: {\n    &#x27;0&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5b&#x27;),\n    &#x27;1&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5c&#x27;),\n    &#x27;2&#x27;: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5d&#x27;)\n  }\n}\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.findOne({ patientID: &quot;P002&quot; })\n{\n  _id: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5c&#x27;),\n  patientID: &#x27;P002&#x27;,\n  name: &#x27;Divya S&#x27;,\n  age: 32,\n  department: &#x27;Neurology&#x27;,\n  admissionDate: ISODate(&#x27;2025-10-20T00:00:00.000Z&#x27;),\n  dischargeDate: ISODate(&#x27;2025-10-28T00:00:00.000Z&#x27;),\n  status: &#x27;discharged&#x27;\n}\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.deleteOne({ patientID: &quot;P002&quot; })\n{ acknowledged: true, deletedCount: 1 }\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.find({ department: &quot;Cardiology&quot; })\n[\n  {\n    _id: ObjectId(&#x27;6b01fd56e237b6b357dd6b5b&#x27;),\n    patientID: &#x27;P001&#x27;,\n    name: &#x27;Arun Kumar&#x27;,\n    age: 45,\n    department: &#x27;Cardiology&#x27;,\n    admissionDate: ISODate(&#x27;2025-11-02T00:00:00.000Z&#x27;),\n    dischargeDate: null,\n    status: &#x27;admitted&#x27;\n  }\n]\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.updateMany({}, { $set: { insuranceProvider: &quot;Not Provided&quot; } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 2,\n  modifiedCount: 2,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.updateOne({ patientID: &quot;P003&quot; }, { $set: { status: &quot;admitted&quot; } })\n{\n  acknowledged: true,\n  insertedId: null,\n  matchedCount: 1,\n  modifiedCount: 1,\n  upsertedCount: 0\n}\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.find({}, { name: 1, department: 1, status: 1, _id: 0 }).sort({ admissionDate: -1 })\n[\n  { name: &#x27;Rahul M&#x27;, department: &#x27;Orthopedics&#x27;, status: &#x27;admitted&#x27; },\n  { name: &#x27;Arun Kumar&#x27;, department: &#x27;Cardiology&#x27;, status: &#x27;admitted&#x27; }\n]\n\nhospitalDB&gt; db.patients.countDocuments({ status: &quot;admitted&quot; })\n2<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li><code>use<\/code> creates the database the moment something is stored in it; <code>createCollection<\/code> creates the collection explicitly (an insert would also create it).<\/li>\n<li><code>updateMany({}, …)<\/code>: the empty filter <code>{}<\/code> matches every document; <code>$set<\/code> adds the field or changes it.<\/li>\n<li>Projection <code>{ name: 1, department: 1, status: 1, _id: 0 }<\/code> shows only those fields; <code>sort({ admissionDate: -1 })<\/code> is descending.<\/li>\n<li>(v) removed the discharged patient P002 and (viii) moved P003 from \"under observation\" to \"admitted\", so (x) counts 2.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "Nov25 Q24": "<p>Express handles the routes; <b>Mongoose<\/b> connects to MongoDB and defines the Student model. Setup: <code>npm init -y<\/code>, then <code>npm install express mongoose<\/code>, start MongoDB, run <code>node server.js<\/code>.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">// server.js\nconst express = require(&quot;express&quot;);\nconst mongoose = require(&quot;mongoose&quot;);\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use(express.json());          // read JSON request bodies\n\n// connect to MongoDB\nmongoose.connect(&quot;mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/universityDB&quot;)\n  .then(() =&gt; console.log(&quot;Connected to MongoDB&quot;))\n  .catch((err) =&gt; console.log(&quot;DB connection error:&quot;, err.message));\n\n// schema and model\nconst studentSchema = new mongoose.Schema({\n  name: { type: String, required: true, unique: true, trim: true },\n  department: { type: String, required: true },\n  cgpa: { type: Number, required: true, min: 0, max: 10 }\n});\nconst Student = mongoose.model(&quot;Student&quot;, studentSchema);\n\n// POST /api/addStudent : add a new student\napp.post(&quot;/api/addStudent&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; {\n  try {\n    const { name, department, cgpa } = req.body;\n    if (!name || !department || cgpa === undefined) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ message: &quot;name, department and cgpa are required&quot; });\n    }\n    const existing = await Student.findOne({ name: name.trim() });\n    if (existing) {\n      return res.status(409).json({ message: &quot;Student with this name already exists&quot; });\n    }\n    const student = new Student({ name, department, cgpa });\n    await student.save();\n    res.status(201).json({ message: &quot;Student added successfully&quot;, student });\n  } catch (err) {\n    res.status(500).json({ message: &quot;Error adding student&quot;, error: err.message });\n  }\n});\n\n// GET /api/viewAllStudents : fetch all students\napp.get(&quot;/api/viewAllStudents&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; {\n  try {\n    const students = await Student.find();\n    res.status(200).json(students);\n  } catch (err) {\n    res.status(500).json({ message: &quot;Error fetching students&quot;, error: err.message });\n  }\n});\n\napp.listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;Server running on http://localhost:3000&quot;));<\/pre>\n<p><b>Testing it<\/b> (Postman, or curl as below), with the real responses:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"out\">$ node server.js\nServer running on http://localhost:3000\nConnected to MongoDB\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ananya R&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;CSE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:8.7}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Student added successfully&quot;,&quot;student&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ananya R&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;CSE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:8.7,&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6b01fd881a88605333c2841b&quot;,&quot;__v&quot;:0}}\n(HTTP 201)\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Karthik S&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;ECE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:7.9}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Student added successfully&quot;,&quot;student&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Karthik S&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;ECE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:7.9,&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6b01fd881a88605333c2841c&quot;,&quot;__v&quot;:0}}\n(HTTP 201)\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ananya R&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;IT&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:9.1}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Student with this name already exists&quot;}\n(HTTP 409)\n\n$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/addStudent -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Meera&quot;}&#x27;\n{&quot;message&quot;:&quot;name, department and cgpa are required&quot;}\n(HTTP 400)\n\n$ curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/viewAllStudents\n[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6b01fd881a88605333c2841b&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ananya R&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;CSE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:8.7,&quot;__v&quot;:0},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6b01fd881a88605333c2841c&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Karthik S&quot;,&quot;department&quot;:&quot;ECE&quot;,&quot;cgpa&quot;:7.9,&quot;__v&quot;:0}]\n(HTTP 200)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Duplicate check<\/b>: before saving, <code>findOne({ name })<\/code> looks for the same name and returns <b>409 Conflict<\/b> with a message. <code>unique: true<\/code> in the schema is a second guard at the database level.<\/li>\n<li><b>Validation<\/b>: missing fields give <b>400 Bad Request<\/b>; the schema enforces types and 0 ≤ CGPA ≤ 10.<\/li>\n<li><b>Error handling<\/b>: each route is wrapped in <code>try/catch<\/code> and returns <b>500<\/b> with the error message if the database fails.<\/li>\n<li>Status codes: 201 Created for a new student, 200 OK for the list.<\/li>\n<\/ul>"};
